# Mockingbird: "You may have this creature enter as a copy of any creature on the battlefield with mana value less than or
# equal to the amount of mana spent to cast this creature, except it's a Bird in addition to its other types and it has
# flying." Bot1 casts it with X = 1: {1}{U} is two mana spent (the {U} counts, not just X), so Thalia (mana value 2,
# equal) and Llanowar Elves (1) are both choices. It enters as Thalia, Guardian of Thraben: a Human Soldier Bird, with first
# strike and the added flying, 2/1. Bot2's Thalia is unchanged and Bot1's copy is a second legendary permanent of
# that name under a different controller, so the legend rule (CR 704.5j) does not apply.

